#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""agent-resume: resurrect a Claude Code teammate into its swarm tmux session.

Usage: agent-resume [<selector>] [options] [-- ...forwarded to claude]

The selector may sit anywhere among the flags: the allowlist records which flags
take a value, so a bare token is either that value or the selector, and position
carries no meaning. Two bare tokens are an error naming both, since one of them
would otherwise reach the resumed session as an unasked-for prompt. Put anything
genuinely meant for claude after `--`, which ends classification.

The bare argument is classified by shape:
    2a38de2d-bd34-...   session UUID       -> --resume
    teammate@session-x  full agent id      -> --agent-id
    session-a52cb2af    a dir under teams/ -> --team (whole roster, lead last)
    teammate            bare agent name    -> resolved, or refused if several rosters claim it

--to-team TEAM|live rebinds a member onto another team: it relaunches the agent
with that team's identity, replaces whichever process still holds the
transcript, registers it in the destination roster and retires the source entry.

--install sets up the ~/.local/bin symlink and zsh tab completion.

Or select explicitly with --agent-id (as claude spells it) and/or --resume <session-uuid>.
Everything the harness needs to relaunch it (team, type, color, model, effort,
permission mode, cwd, parent session, tmux socket + pane) is reconstructed from
three on-disk sources plus the live process table; when they disagree, the most
recent value wins.

Flags for the resumed session are an allowlist, PASSTHROUGH_FLAGS, not a
passthrough, and a forwarded flag overrides the value this tool would have
derived. The allowlist is what lets a misspelling of one of our own flags be
caught instead of reaching claude as an unknown argument: a run given --dry-ryn
read as though it had honoured a dry run it never saw.

The cost is maintenance. The list is hand-held, so a flag claude grows is
refused here until the table learns it, and the newer ones churn. It is not
derived from `claude --help` because that costs most of a second per run and
omits --agent-id, --agent-name, --team-name and --parent-session-id, which are
real and are precisely the flags this tool exists to set.
"""

